      "body": "Fixes #48875.\n\nAdds an errata note to the Hardware Requirements section of the batch-invariance docs: Ampere (SM 8.x) support landed in #38427 and shipped in v0.20.0, while the v0.20.0 through v0.22.0 documentation incorrectly stated \"9.0 or higher\" for NVIDIA GPUs.\n\nWhy this is not a duplicate: #48875 is open with no linked PR addressing it. I checked the issue's comment thread and searched open PRs referencing the issue before writing this.\n\nValidation: docs-only change, no tests applicable. Verified the claim against the code (`vllm/model_executor/determinism/batch_invariant.py` enables the batch-invariant Triton matmul when `is_device_capability_family(80)`, which is true for all SM 8.x) and confirmed #38427 is merged (merge commit `16a65e417`).\n\nAI assistance: this PR was prepared with AI assistance. The full diff was shared with the human submitter for review before opening.",
